{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>From his youth.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory said: 'from his youth' — from the time he is shaken loose to emerge from his mother's womb. And it is known that a person is not held liable for commandments, which pertain to the side of the good impulse (yetzer ha-tov), until thirteen years; and this is what our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded: the evil impulse (yetzer ha-ra) is greater than the good impulse for thirteen years. And thus Solomon, peace be upon him, said (Ecclesiastes 4:14): ״כי מבית הסורים יצא למלוך״ — 'for out of the house of prisoners he goes forth to reign' — for from the moment he emerges from the house of the womb, where he is confined and closed up like a man imprisoned in a prison, immediately he wants to reign, and he seeks the opening of the breach (פי הדד) and is drawn after desires. And because the word is spelled without an alef (חסרה אל\"ף), they interpreted it in the sense of the Targum, for the Targum of ויבאש is וסרי."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "The phrase 'פי הדד' is translated hyper-literally ('opening of the breach'); the expression is unusual and possibly textually uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:11:21.359008989Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}